#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Found an integer-indexed aggregation reference but this stage has no `aggregation:` clause"
msgstr "Fandt en integer-indekseret aggregeringsreference, men denne stage har ingen `aggregation:`-klausul"

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Detected a post-aggregation filter alongside `order-by:`, `limit:`, or `fields:` in the same stage. MBQL 5 requires the filter in a separate stage, but those trailing clauses cannot be safely relocated — they may reference pre-aggregation columns that don''t survive the split. Please author this as two stages explicitly: stage 0 with `source-table`, `aggregation`, `breakout`, and any pre-aggregation `filters`; stage 1 with the post-aggregation `filters`, plus `order-by` / `limit` / `fields` that reference the aggregation''s output via cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` refs."
msgstr "Opdagede et post-aggregeringsfilter sammen med `order-by:`, `limit:` eller `fields:` i samme fase. MBQL 5 kræver, at filteret ligger i en separat fase, men disse efterfølgende klausuler kan ikke flyttes sikkert — de kan referere til præ-aggregeringskolonner, som ikke overlever opdelingen. Skriv dette eksplicit som to faser: fase 0 med `source-table`, `aggregation`, `breakout` og eventuelle præ-aggregerings-`filters`; fase 1 med post-aggregerings-`filters` plus `order-by` / `limit` / `fields`, der refererer til aggregeringens output via refs på tværs af faser `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]`."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Detected a post-aggregation filter (a filter referencing an aggregation from the same stage). MBQL 5 requires this in a separate stage. Auto-fix is unsafe here — either an aggregation''s output column name cannot be derived (e.g. a `metric` reference or unknown head), or two aggregations in this stage would produce the same column name (e.g. two `sum` aggregations on different fields, which lib disambiguates as `sum` / `sum_2` based on field order). Please refactor to multi-stage manually: put the aggregations in stage 0, and the filter in stage 1 referencing the column via a cross-stage `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]` clause. Use an explicit aggregation with a `name` opts override (e.g. `[\"sum\", (opts with key \"name\" → \"sum_total\"), …]`) if you need stable cross-stage names."
msgstr "Opdagede et post-aggregeringsfilter (et filter der refererer til en aggregering fra samme fase). MBQL 5 kræver dette i en separat fase. Auto-fix er usikkert her — enten kan et output-kolonnenavn for en aggregering ikke udledes (f.eks. en `metric`-reference eller ukendt head), eller to aggregeringer i denne fase ville give samme kolonnenavn (f.eks. to `sum`-aggregeringer på forskellige felter, som biblioteket adskiller som `sum` / `sum_2` baseret på feltrækkefølge). Refaktorer venligst manuelt til flere faser: læg aggregeringerne i fase 0, og filteret i fase 1, som refererer til kolonnen via en klausul på tværs af faser `[\"field\", (empty opts), \"<column-name>\"]`. Brug en eksplicit aggregering med en `name` opts-override (f.eks. `[\"sum\", (opts med nøglen \"name\" → \"sum_total\"), …]`), hvis du har brug for stabile navne på tværs af faser."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} is on table {1}, which has no foreign key from the source table {2}, so it cannot be reached implicitly. To group or filter by a column from that table, add an explicit `joins:` entry and reference the field using the join alias. If you are aggregating a metric that relates to that table (metrics can join tables that have no foreign key), read that metric dimensions resource `metabase://metric/<metric_id>/dimensions` which lists the exact join clause to paste into `joins:` and the columns it unlocks. Otherwise use a field from the source table."
msgstr "Felt {0} ligger på tabellen {1}, som ikke har nogen fremmednøgle fra kildetabellen {2}, så det kan ikke nås implicit. For at gruppere eller filtrere efter en kolonne fra den tabel skal du tilføje en eksplicit `joins:`-post og referere til feltet ved hjælp af join-aliaset. Hvis du aggregerer en metrik, der relaterer til den tabel (metrikker kan join'e tabeller, der ikke har nogen fremmednøgle), så læs metrik-dimensionerressourcen `metabase://metric/<metric_id>/dimensions`, som viser den præcise join-klausul, der skal indsættes i `joins:`, og de kolonner, den låser op for. Ellers skal du bruge et felt fra kildetabellen."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} can be reached from {1} via {2} foreign keys. Specify the `source-field` option on the field clause to disambiguate; call `read_resource` with `metabase://table/<numeric id>/fields` for the source table to list the available foreign-key columns."
msgstr "Felt {0} kan nås fra {1} via {2} fremmednøgler. Angiv indstillingen `source-field` på feltklausulen for at afklare; kald `read_resource` med `metabase://table/<numeric id>/fields` for kildetabellen for at liste de tilgængelige fremmednøglekolonner."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Field {0} is reachable from {1} explicit joins via aliases {2}. Specify the `source-field-join-alias` option on the field clause to pick which join''s foreign key to use."
msgstr "Felt {0} kan nås fra {1} eksplicitte joins via aliasser {2}. Angiv `source-field-join-alias`-optionen på field-klausulen for at vælge, hvilken joins fremmednøgle der skal bruges."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "No column named {0} is available to reference in this stage. Reference a column by its machine name (e.g. an aggregation is `max`, `count`, `sum` - never its display label like `Max of X`), not a UI label. Available column names: {1}."
msgstr "Der er ingen kolonne med navnet {0}, som kan refereres til i dette trin. Referér til en kolonne med dens maskinnavn (f.eks. er en aggregering `max`, `count`, `sum` – aldrig dens visningsetiket som `Max of X`), ikke en UI-etiket. Tilgængelige kolonnenavne: {1}."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "Stage {0} aggregation entry {1} is a `field` clause, not an aggregation. The `aggregation:` block expects aggregation functions like `count`, `sum`, `avg`, `metric`, etc. - or wrap the field in one (e.g. `[sum, <opts>, <field>]`). If you wanted to group by this column, use `breakout:` instead."
msgstr "Stage {0} aggregeringsentry {1} er en `field`-klausul, ikke en aggregering. `aggregation:`-blokken forventer aggregeringsfunktioner som `count`, `sum`, `avg`, `metric` osv. - eller pak feltet ind i en (f.eks. `[sum, <opts>, <field>]`). Hvis du ville gruppere efter denne kolonne, så brug `breakout:` i stedet."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`case` (and `if`) uses its third positional argument as the fallback value, not a `default` key in the options map. Move the value out of the options map and append it as the third arg of the clause: `[case, <opts>, <branch-pairs>, <default>]`. Omit the third arg entirely if you have no fallback (the result will be null on miss)."
msgstr "`case` (og `if`) bruger sin tredje positionsargument som fallback-værdi, ikke en `default`-nøgle i options-mappet. Flyt værdien ud af options-mappet, og tilføj den som tredje arg i klausulen: `[case, <opts>, <branch-pairs>, <default>]`. Udelad helt tredje arg, hvis du ikke har nogen fallback (resultatet bliver null ved miss)."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`{0}` is not a clause in repr; it was a top-level operation in the older sexp pipeline. {1}"
msgstr "`{0}` er ikke en klausul i repr; det var en top-level-operation i den ældre sexp-pipeline. {1}"

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`[expression, <opts>, <name>]` reference requires a non-blank string identifier in the third slot, matching an entry in some stage''s `expressions:` block."
msgstr "`[expression, <opts>, <name>]`-reference kræver en ikke-tom strengidentifikator i tredje slot, der matcher en entry i en stages `expressions:`-blok."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "`field` clause needs a portable FK in its third slot, not a numeric id. Use a vector `[<database>, <schema>, <table>, <column>]` (resolved against the metadata provider) or a string column-name (for cross-stage references)."
msgstr "`field`-klausulen kræver en portabel FK i tredje slot, ikke et numerisk id. Brug en vektor `[<database>, <schema>, <table>, <column>]` (slået op mod metadata-provideren) eller et kolonnenavn som streng (til referencer på tværs af stages)."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/repair.clj
msgid "The query builder''s expression editor rejects a {0} clause in stage {1}: {2}. The query would build but could not be visualized or saved - rewrite the offending clause."
msgstr "Forespørgselsbyggerens udtrykseditor afviser en {0}-klausul i trin {1}: {2}. Forespørgslen kunne bygges, men kunne ikke visualiseres eller gemmes – omskriv den problematiske klausul."

#: metabase/agent_lib/representations/resolve.clj
msgid "Invalid temporal literal {0} in :absolute-datetime — use an ISO-8601 date, datetime, year, or year-month."
msgstr "Ugyldig tidslig literal {0} i :absolute-datetime — brug en ISO-8601-dato, datetime, år eller år-måned."

#: metabase/ai_tracing/api.clj
msgid "Eval trace not found"
msgstr "Eval-trace blev ikke fundet"

#: metabase/ai_tracing/settings.clj
msgid "Enable eval-time AI agent trace capture. When true, agent / MCP / agent-api runs capture a full trace (prompts, completions, tool I/O, custom spans) and write it as structured JSONL to a per-session file via the dedicated `metabase.ai-tracing.log` logger. Separate from MB_TRACING_ENABLED. Off by default; intended for dedicated eval instances, NOT production (traces contain full, unredacted user content)."
msgstr "Aktivér eval-time AI-agent trace-opsamling. Når true, opsamler agent / MCP / agent-api-kørsler en fuld trace (prompts, completions, tool I/O, custom spans) og skriver den som struktureret JSONL til en fil pr. session via den dedikerede `metabase.ai-tracing.log` logger. Adskilt fra MB_TRACING_ENABLED. Slået fra som standard; beregnet til dedikerede eval-instanser, IKKE produktion (traces indeholder fuldt, uredigeret brugerindhold)."

